# Line endings for files a Linux container has to parse.
#
# Scoped deliberately rather than `* text=auto eol=lf` repo-wide. Everything
# below fails *silently* at runtime on the wrong endings and passes every local
# check: a shell script with CRLF dies at CMD with '\r: not found', and an nginx
# config with CRLF is rejected at startup for a directive it read correctly.
#
# Git normalises line endings when diffing, so a CRLF working-tree file can sit
# there looking clean in `git status` and `git diff` while being broken in the
# image. It happened here: a script that rewrote these files with Python's
# default text mode converted frontend/nginx.conf to CRLF, and nothing in the
# repo said so.
#
# The Caddyfile is here for the same reason as nginx.conf. It is mounted into
# the edge container as the site configuration, and Caddy rejects a config
# file with a stray carriage return: the container dies on boot with a parse
# error that names neither the file nor the line.
#
# Deliberately NOT listed: *.yml, *.sql, *.ini and the Python sources. CRLF is
# harmless in all of them - YAML and INI parsers strip it, and Python handles
# universal newlines - so forcing it would create diff noise for no benefit.

*.sh    text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
**/Dockerfile   text eol=lf
nginx.conf      text eol=lf
**/nginx.conf   text eol=lf
Caddyfile      text eol=lf
**/Caddyfile   text eol=lf